<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F20.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 20</span>: </span><span id="A1.F20.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Parameter summary for Bellman Ford MinAggGNN without self-loops (<a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Bellman-Ford without Self-Loops ‣ Appendix A Additional Results for Bellman-Ford ‣ MINAR: Mechanistic Interpretability for Neural Algorithmic Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Results on SALSA-CLRS</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we provide additional results from <a href="#S6" title="6 Case Study: SALSA-CLRS ‣ MINAR: Mechanistic Interpretability for Neural Algorithmic Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, including separate fidelity metrics (<a href="#A2.F21" title="In Appendix B Additional Results on SALSA-CLRS ‣ MINAR: Mechanistic Interpretability for Neural Algorithmic Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>), circuit accuracy and ablations on each task (<a href="#A2.F22" title="In Appendix B Additional Results on SALSA-CLRS ‣ MINAR: Mechanistic Interpretability for Neural Algorithmic Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>), and circuit overlap for each scoring method across all values of <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#A2.F23" title="In Appendix B Additional Results on SALSA-CLRS ‣ MINAR: Mechanistic Interpretability for Neural Algorithmic Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>, <a href="#A2.F24" title="In Appendix B Additional Results on SALSA-CLRS ‣ MINAR: Mechanistic Interpretability for Neural Algorithmic Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F21" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.21442v1/fidelity_circuit_ablate_vs_K_l1_lr=0.001_eta=0.001_weight_decay=0.1.svg" id="A2.F21.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/132;" width="476" height="132"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F21.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 21</span>: </span><math id="A2.F21.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Fid}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext mathsize="0.900em">Fid</mtext><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Fid}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.F21.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (top) and <math id="A2.F21.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Fid}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext>Fid</mtext><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Fid}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> (bottom) for SALSA-CLRS circuits using Weight, <span id="A2.F21.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">WeightGrad</span>, EAP, and EAP-IG (<math id="A2.F21.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=20</annotation></semantics></math>) at <math id="A2.F21.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\{10,25,50,100,250,500,1000,1500,2000,2500\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>250</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1500</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2000</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2500</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\{10,25,50,100,250,500,1000,1500,2000,2500\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A2.F21.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Fid}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext>Fid</mtext><mo>−</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Fid}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>, lower indicates a more sufficient circuit. For <math id="A2.F21.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Fid}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext>Fid</mtext><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Fid}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, higher indicates a more necessary circuit.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F22" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.21442v1/accuracy_circuit_ablate_vs_K_l1_lr=0.001_eta=0.001_weight_decay=0.1.svg" id="A2.F22.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/132;" width="476" height="132"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F22.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 22</span>: </span><span id="A2.F22.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Circuit accuracy (top) and ablated accuracy (bottom) for SALSA-CLRS circuits using Weight, <span id="A2.F22.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">WeightGrad</span>, EAP, and EAP-IG (<math id="A2.F22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=20</annotation></semantics></math>) at <math id="A2.F22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\{10,25,50,100,250,500,1000,1500,2000,2500,3000\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>250</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1500</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2000</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2500</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3000</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\{10,25,50,100,250,500,1000,1500,2000,2500,3000\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For circuit accuracy, higher is better. For ablated accuracy, lower indicates a necessary circuit.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.F23" class="ltx_figure ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:171.2pt;height:550pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><div class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="width:550.0pt;transform:translate(-189.4pt,-189.4pt) rotate(-90deg) ;"><figure><img src="2602.21442v1/jaccard_indices_all_scores_lr=0.001_eta=0.001_weight_decay=0.1_1.png" id="A2.F23.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/217;" width="476" height="217" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F23.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 23</span>: </span><span id="A2.F23.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Weighted Jaccard index between CLRS circuits using <span id="A2.F23.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">WeightGrad</span>, EAP, and EAP-IG (<math id="A2.F23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=20</annotation></semantics></math>) at <math id="A2.F23.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\{10,25,50,100,250,500\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>250</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>500</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\{10,25,50,100,250,500\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<div id="A2.F24" class="ltx_figure ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:198.5pt;height:550pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><div class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="width:550.0pt;transform:translate(-175.8pt,-175.8pt) rotate(-90deg) ;"><figure><img src="2602.21442v1/jaccard_indices_all_scores_lr=0.001_eta=0.001_weight_decay=0.1_2.png" id="A2.F24.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/254;" width="476" height="254" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F24.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 24</span>: </span><span id="A2.F24.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Weighted Jaccard index between CLRS circuits using <span id="A2.F24.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">WeightGrad</span>, EAP, and EAP-IG (<math id="A2.F24.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=20</annotation></semantics></math>) at <math id="A2.F24.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\{1000,1500,2000,2500,3000\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1500</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2000</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2500</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3000</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\{1000,1500,2000,2500,3000\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Training Data</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Shortest Path Data</h3>

<figure id="A3.F25" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.21442v1/training.svg" id="A3.F25.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/130;" width="476" height="130"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F25.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 25</span>: </span><span id="A3.F25.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Training graphs for the Bellman-Ford MinAggGNN from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nerem et al., 2025</a>]</cite>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nerem et al., 2025</a>]</cite>, we construct a training set <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\text{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\text{train}}</annotation></semantics></math> from the graphs depicted in <a href="#A3.F25" title="In C.1 Shortest Path Data ‣ Appendix C Training Data ‣ MINAR: Mechanistic Interpretability for Neural Algorithmic Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a> for <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=2</annotation></semantics></math>. It includes all path graphs of the form <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{K+1}^{(1)}(a,\dots,b,\dots,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{K+1}^{(1)}(a,\dots,b,\dots,0)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in\{0,1,\dots,2K\}\times\{0,\dots,2K+1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\in\{0,1,\dots,2K\}\times\{0,\dots,2K+1\}</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> is the weight of the <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>-th edge). It also includes the graph <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{K}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{K}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> from <a href="#A3.F25" title="In C.1 Shortest Path Data ‣ Appendix C Training Data ‣ MINAR: Mechanistic Interpretability for Neural Algorithmic Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a> and the special path graphs <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}^{(0)}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}^{(0)}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{2}^{(1)}(1,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{2}^{(1)}(1,0)</annotation></semantics></math>. We also include extra path graphs: four three-node path graphs initialized at step zero of Bellman-Ford and four four-node path graphs initialized at step two of Bellman-Ford, each with randomly generated edge weights.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the out-of-distribution test set, we include a collection of 3 and 4-node cycle graphs; complete graphs on 5 to 200 nodes; and Erdős-Rényi graphs on 5 to 200 nodes with <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>. To provide extra examples of graphs with unreachable nodes, we also generate binary and ternary trees of depths of 3 and 4. All test graphs have randomly generated edge weights, and the test set contains 300 graphs in total.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The corrupted dataset includes feature-ablated versions of every graph in the test dataset. An example is given in <a href="#A3.F26" title="In C.1 Shortest Path Data ‣ Appendix C Training Data ‣ MINAR: Mechanistic Interpretability for Neural Algorithmic Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>.</p>
</div>
